{#
    "Deploying X on-device" section for GenieX models. Call sites must guard
    on has_geniex_runtime. needs_local_export adds the export-to-local-path
    line for models whose artifacts cannot be redistributed (i.e.
    restrict_model_sharing), so the user must run the export step themselves.
    has_genie_runtime adds the Genie deprecation note.
#}
{%- macro deploying_on_device(
    model_name,
    needs_local_export,
    has_genie_runtime,
    geniex_url,
    geniex_quickstart_url,
    genie_url
) -%}
## Deploying {{ model_name }} on-device

Follow the [GenieX quickstart]({{ geniex_quickstart_url }}) to install GenieX and deploy the model on a target device.
{% if needs_local_export %}

You'll need to export the model artifact using the steps below, then follow [Run a Local Model with GenieX]({{ geniex_url }}).
{% endif %}
{% if has_genie_runtime %}

See the [LLM-on-Genie]({{ genie_url }}) tutorial to run with the Genie runtime. Note: Genie support will be deprecated soon.
{% endif %}
{%- endmacro -%}


